  "question": {
    "text": "In an equilateral triangle <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></math> equation of the side <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and the centroid of&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> are in anticlockwise order, then the equation of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
